--- body ---
## Context
Child of 1164 (Stopguard, deferred), author's decision 2026-10-27: instead of Stopguard's phase 1 (a dry-run
end-of-turn hook, 3.5 agent-h + 0.3 author-h), measure the two bad stops after the fact from session traces and let
the trace-doctor's monthly survey report them. This yields 1164's gate G1 (>= 5 bad stops per week on Claude Code)
with no hook in the turn path (Monitor, not guard).

Bad stops (conception/2026-10-21-stopguard-design.md):
1. ask without ask-up: a turn that ends on a question to the author with no advisor call earlier in that turn,
   excluding decisions that are the author's by right where they can be recognised;
2. wait without wake: a turn that ends saying it waits while no background task, timer or watcher is pending.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A script reads the session traces the trace-doctor already reads and counts each bad stop per week, per runtime
      where the traces allow, listing the offending turns.
- [ ] Precision checked against a hand-labelled sample (at least 30 turns, including positive controls from the
      2026-10-27 raid session); precision and recall stated; heuristic limits documented.
- [ ] The trace-doctor survey reports the weekly counts and names 1164's G1 threshold.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

Related: [[1164]].

## Imagine (raid 2026-10-27b)
- Premise check: holds. No stopguard code exists (`scripts/` has no stop_guard); 1164 is still deferred and
  conception/2026-10-21-stopguard-design.md §6 phase 3 (Claude Code replay, G1) is the sibling this replaces. Since
  2026-10-21 only review-chain work (1273-1281) touched scripts/; nothing on trace-*.py or skills/trace-doctor.
- Simplest path: one new standard-library script `scripts/trace-stopguard.py`, a sibling of trace-wall-time.py,
  reusing its trace walk (importlib-load pattern; `_load_records`, `load_traces`, sub-agents excluded) and the
  `--days/--projects-dir/--json` flags. A turn = records from a human prompt to the last assistant `end_turn`
  record. Rule 1: last text block's final non-empty line outside a code fence ends in `?`, and no Agent/SendMessage
  call (the advisor) earlier in that turn; AskUserQuestion-ended turns count as asks. Rule 2: final text matches a
  wait vocabulary (design §3 list) while no pending background Bash/Agent/Monitor/ScheduleWakeup (tool_use with no
  later task-notification or end) exists. Weekly bucket by ISO week of the turn end.
  YAGNI: no spool, hook, registry or Turn class (design §3-4 is the hook this ticket replaces); no Codex/Pi walker
  (their traces are another format, ~6 and ~5 weeks; report "claude-code only, others unmeasured", which the
  criterion allows with "where the traces allow"); no automatic labeller, the sample is hand-labelled.
  Premature-abstraction risk: do not factor a shared trace-reader module; copy-load as wall-time does.
- Risk class: judgment (heuristic rules with a precision/recall claim and an author-by-right exclusion list).
  Suggested coder: opus. The hand-labelling cannot be done by the author in-run; see mapping.

## Plan
1. `scripts/trace-stopguard.py`: `iter_turns(traces)`, `rule_ask_up(turn)`, `rule_wait(turn)`, `by_week`, argparse `--days`,
   `--json`, `--list` (offending turns: session id, ts, last 160 chars; no full text, none committed).
2. `tests/test_trace_stopguard.py`: synthetic-trace fixtures in the `_use/_res/_say` style of test_trace_wall_time.py.
3. `skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md`: add the script to § 1 survey block (a seventh script, run beside wall-time, output
   `$SCRATCH/stopguard.json`) and a short "Bad stops" subsection in § 2 reporting weekly counts per runtime and
   naming "1164 gate G1: >= 5 bad stops per week on Claude Code: reopen; below: close". Bump "six" to "seven".
4. `conception/2026-10-27-stopguard-measure-labels.md`: the hand-labelled sample (turn id = session:index, label,
   one line; no message text) with precision, recall and documented limits. Update conception only; do not edit 1164.
- First test: `test_ask_up_flags_question_without_advisor`: two turns ending "Which one?"; one has an earlier Agent
  call to the advisor; assert only the other is flagged. Catches a wrong implementation that flags any "?" or
  ignores the advisor, and the sibling `test_question_in_code_fence_and_mid_message_not_flagged`; the wait test
  pairs a pending `run_in_background` with and without a task-notification (a tautological "flags the word
  waiting" implementation fails the paired case).
- Files touched: scripts/trace-stopguard.py (new), tests/test_trace_stopguard.py (new), skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md,
  conception/2026-10-27-stopguard-measure-labels.md (new). Registries: none edited (trace scripts are not listed in a
  dispatch table; run `make skills-catalog` only if the description changes, it should not). tests/fixtures/harness-doctor/trace-doctor-SKILL.md
  is a frozen sha-pinned control: do NOT touch it.
- Dependencies: none open (1282-1292, 1252, 1277 do not touch trace-* or trace-doctor). Soft: 1164 (read-only).
  File overlap: only skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md, shared with no listed ticket.
- Exit mapping: (1) script + tests, step 1-2; claude-code only, other runtimes stated unmeasured. (2) Precision/recall:
  agent draws >= 30 turns (>= 10 flagged, >= 10 unflagged, the positives from today's raid session ~/.claude traces, e.g.
  turns ending in a question to the author) and proposes labels; the AUTHOR must confirm the labels (agent cannot
  know "would have preferred to continue"). Coder reports precision/recall as "agent-labelled, pending author
  confirmation" and lists the 30 for a 0.2 author-hour skim; exit stays unticked until confirmed. Recall = flagged
  among labelled-bad of an unflagged sample, with the small-n interval stated. (3) step 3. (4) `make check` / the
  scoped gate (.idh-checks.json), quoting selected/skipped.
- Decide (orchestrator): accept agent-labelled-then-author-skim as discharging criterion 2, or hold the ticket open
  for the author. Recommended: accept the skim (0.2 author-h) rather than 1.5 author-h of fresh labelling.

